# Next.js Conventions (App Router Only)

## Only Use App Router
- **Only use the App Router** (`/app` or `/src/app` directories). 
- Do not use the legacy `pages/` directory.

## Explicit File-Based Routes
Routing for entities must follow **explicit file-based routes**:
- `/app/entity/create/page.tsx` → creation form  
- `/app/entity/[id]/page.tsx` or `/app/entity/[slug]/page.tsx` → detail view  
- `/app/entity/[id]/update/page.tsx` → update form  
- `/app/entity/[id]/manage/page.tsx` → management view  
- (same conventions apply if project uses `/src/app` instead of `/app`)

## No State Multiplexing
- **Do not** multiplex create/edit/show/manage states inside a single route. 
- Routing must represent application state clearly.

## Server Components by Default
- Use **server components by default**, and introduce client components only when stateful interactivity is required.
